 "notes": "Curve is the lower boundary of the red 'PSI-HgM-sideband' 95% C.L. exclusion patch in Fig. 4, read directly from the MATLAB figure file Images/AxionWindLimits221122_F1.fig shipped in the arXiv e-print (vertices of the FaceColor=[0.7 0.1 0.3] patch; verified against the published AxionWindLimits230313_F1.png). Paper plots g_aNN in GeV^-1 vs Compton frequency f_a; converted with m_a = h f_a and, per the 2m_N rule, g_an = 2 m_n g_aNN (paper Eq. 3: L = g_aNN dmu(a) psibar gamma^mu gamma5 psi, equal neutron/proton couplings assumed; 199Hg is predominantly neutron-sensitive, so reported as the axion-neutron coupling with g_ap implicitly set to zero). Main red region assumes instantaneous B.p orientation; the alternative dash-dotted cyan curve using the time-averaged orientation <B.p>=0.7 is exactly a factor 1/0.7 higher and matches the abstract's quoted peak sensitivity g_aNN~3.5e-6 GeV^-1 (red-region peak is 2.47e-6 GeV^-1, i.e. g_an=4.6e-6). rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed. Downsampled from 120 patch vertices with RDP in log-log space; insensitive blind spots at multiples of f_Hg=7.879 Hz are not depicted in the paper's figure and hence not excised here.",
